BrickNext

BrickNext is a noncommercial adaptation of NextUI for the TrimUI Brick,
maintained by retrotiv. It exists to add an integrated music player (AnberTunes)
and retrotiv's own touches on top of NextUI, and to keep working even if an
upstream project goes away.

Credits and upstream projects:

- NextUI - by LoveRetro (https://github.com/LoveRetro/NextUI), the firmware
  BrickNext is built on. NextUI is itself based on MinUI by Shaun Inman.
  Licensed under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (see LICENSE).
- The emulator cores and standalone emulators (PPSSPP, Flycast, mupen64plus and
  the libretro cores) belong to their respective authors and keep their own
  licenses and notices.
- The heavy-emulator paks (N64, DC, PSP) are by their original authors; BrickNext
  only adds the music-card hooks to their launchers.
- AnberTunes is retrotiv's fork of Boombrick.

BrickNext is noncommercial: donations (ko-fi.com/retrotiv) are welcome, selling it
is not. All trademarks and code above belong to their respective owners.
